Then by the Law of Cosines on Triangle $ADE$,
\[x^2 = x^2 + (10 - x)^2 - 2x(10 - x) \cos A = x^2 + (10 - x)^2 - 2x(10 - x) \cdot \frac{7}{25}.\]Then
\[(10 - x)^2 - 2x(10 - x) \cdot \frac{7}{25} = 0.\]Since $x \neq 10,$ we can divide both sides by $10 - x,$ to get
\[10 - x - 2x \cdot \frac{7}{25} = 0.\]Solving, we find $x = \boxed{\frac{250}{39}}.$

To find the sum, we look at the first few powers of 2 modulo 7: \begin{align*}
2^0 &\equiv 1, \\
2^1 &\equiv 2, \\
2^2 &\equiv 4, \\
2^3 &\equiv 8 \equiv 1 \pmod{7}
\end{align*}Since $2^3 \equiv 1 \pmod{7}$, the powers of 2 modulo 7 repeat in cycles of 3.  Therefore, \begin{align*}
&1 + 2 + 2^2 + 2^3 + \dots + 2^{100} \\
&\quad\equiv 1 + 2 + 4 + 1 + 2 + 4 + \dots + 1 + 2 + 4 + 1 + 2 \\
&\quad\equiv (1 + 2 + 4) + (1 + 2 + 4) + \dots + (1 + 2 + 4) + 1 + 2 \\
&\quad\equiv \boxed{3} \pmod{7}.
\end{align*}

